# CODEOWNERS — mandatory reviewers for TAK-PluginSuite-FeatureLink.
#
# Closes the "no CODEOWNERS" gap (Appendix E §7). The specific risk it addresses: the
# cross-cutting contract files — CONFIG-FORMAT.md and AUTO-ICONSET-SPEC.md — are depended on
# by all seven components, and had no mandatory reviewer at all. A change to either can
# silently break four implementations the author never opened.
#
# CODEOWNERS only has teeth when branch protection requires review from code owners.
# See CONTRIBUTING.md § "Branch protection" for the settings that must be enabled.
#
# !! PLACEHOLDER OWNERS !!
# @featurelink-maintainers and the team handles below DO NOT EXIST yet. GitHub silently
# ignores an unresolvable owner, so this file is inert until real accounts or teams are
# substituted. Replacing them is an owner action tracked in QUESTIONS-FOR-OWNER.md (WP5).
# Until then, treat the assignments as documentation of intent, not as an enforced control.

# ── Default ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*                                   @featurelink-maintainers

# ── Cross-cutting interop contracts — the highest-leverage files in the repo ──
# A change here alters behaviour in five independent implementations across four languages
# (Java x2, TypeScript, C#, Python) shipping on independent release cadences.
/CONFIG-FORMAT.md                   @featurelink-maintainers @featurelink-contract-owners
/AUTO-ICONSET-SPEC.md               @featurelink-maintainers @featurelink-contract-owners
/VERSIONING.md                      @featurelink-maintainers @featurelink-contract-owners
/VERSION                            @featurelink-maintainers @featurelink-contract-owners

# ── Security, privacy and licensing posture ──────────────────────────────────
# PRIVACY.md governs what leaves a responder's device. It is not a docs change.
/SECURITY.md                        @featurelink-maintainers @featurelink-security
/PRIVACY.md                         @featurelink-maintainers @featurelink-security
/LICENSE                            @featurelink-maintainers
/NOTICE                             @featurelink-maintainers
/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md             @featurelink-maintainers

# ── Build, CI and supply chain ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# A change to a workflow can exfiltrate every secret the pipeline holds; a change to a
# pinned digest can substitute code that executes inside the release build.
/.github/                           @featurelink-maintainers @featurelink-security
/.github/workflows/                 @featurelink-maintainers @featurelink-security
/.github/pinned-binaries.sha256     @featurelink-maintainers @featurelink-security
/.gitattributes                     @featurelink-maintainers
/.gitignore                         @featurelink-maintainers

# ── Signing and secrets adjacency ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Any change touching signing configuration needs a security reviewer, not just a build one.
**/app/build.gradle                 @featurelink-maintainers @featurelink-security
**/featurelink.keystore             @featurelink-maintainers @featurelink-security

# ── Per-component ownership ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ATAK 5.6 and 5.7 are forks of one another; so are WinTAK 5.6 and 5.7. Any fix to one MUST
# be applied to the other unless the divergence is deliberate and documented — the PR
# template carries the checklist that enforces this by review.
/ATAK5.6/                           @featurelink-atak
/ATAK5.7/                           @featurelink-atak
/WinTAK5.6/                         @featurelink-wintak
/WinTAK5.7/                         @featurelink-wintak
/CloudTAK/                          @featurelink-cloudtak
/TAKPortal/                         @featurelink-server
/Infra-TAK/                         @featurelink-server

# ── The shared OAuth relay ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This single page serves BOTH CloudTAK and TAK Portal. It is the C-01 site: a change here
# affects the authorization-code flow for two components at once.
/docs/featurelink-oauth-relay.html  @featurelink-maintainers @featurelink-security

# ── Icon corpora ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Two byte-identical 7,461-file copies. Nothing but review and the CI parity job stops them
# from diverging, and divergence breaks the iconset UID contract silently.
/TAKPortal/assets/featurelink-configurator/icons/    @featurelink-maintainers
/Infra-TAK/featurelink_displayconfig_assets/icons/   @featurelink-maintainers
